this is a very active investigation and  it will be for several hours as police  try to piece together exactly what  happened out here around midnight they  were called here at a baby's Ford Road  about someone who was hit by a car and  when they got here that's when the shots  started to ring out  police say nine people were hit by  bullets two people are dead and five  others were hit by cars as they tried to  run away from the scene there was a very  large crowd out here police say this  started as an impromptu block party and  it began Friday as a Juneteenth  celebration that was sort of just a  continuation into the weekend  emotions understandably high out here  this morning we've seen some of the  large crowds leave the area though there  are hundreds of evidence markers  scattered throughout several crime  scenes in parking lots of different  businesses along Beatty's for the road  crime scene units are out here working  to collect evidence and process the  scenes we had the chance to speak with  current chief deputy Johnny Jennings who  will take over the see MPD Police  Department in September he says what  happened here is a tragedy just  continued on in tonight and police say  they have reason to believe that there  may be more than one shooter involved in  what happened out here they also say the  numbers as far as the people who were  injured they could rise throughout the  morning I'm Anne Wyatt little reporting  in Charlotte
 

